arget \"\\\"<self>/canvas/<i>/content\\\"\" ; environment.etc.<self>-canvas-<i>-content.text \"\\\"<value>\\\"\"\n0.9 r4 match fact button.<i> => environment.etc.<self>-button-<i>-label.target \"\\\"<self>/button/<i>/label\\\"\" ; environment.etc.<self>-button-<i>-label.text \"\\\"<value>\\\"\"\n0.9 r5 match fact button.<i>.action => environment.etc.<self>-button-<i>-action.target \"\\\"<self>/button/<i>/action\\\"\" ; environment.etc.<self>-button-<i>-action.text \"\\\"<value>\\\"\"\n0.8 r6 match fact canvas.<i> => clause.website-index-text \"(define (website-index-text) \\\"<!doctype html><html lang='de'><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>website</title><style>body{font-family:sans-serif;margin:2rem} svg.canvas{border:1px solid #333;background:#fff} figcaption{color:#666;font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.3rem} #controls{margin-top:1rem} #controls button{margin-right:.5rem;padding:.4rem .8rem}</style></head><body><div id='stage'></div><div id='controls'></div><script src='app.js'></script></body></html>\\\")\"\n0.95 q1 demand site.port \"on which port should the website be served?\"\n0.85 q2 demand canvas.<i>.content \"what does this canvas show?\"\n0.85 q3 demand button.<i>.action \"what happens when this button is clicked?\"\n0.95 a1 expect services.nginx.defaultHTTPListenPort from site.port\n0.9 a2 expect environment.etc.<self>-canvas-<i>-name.text from canvas.<i>\n0.9 a3 expect environment.etc.<self>-canvas-<i>-content.text from canvas.<i>.content\n0.9 a4 expect environment.etc.<self>-button-<i>-label.text from button.<i>\n0.9 a5 expect environment.etc.<self>-button-<i>-action.text from button.<i>.action\n0.8 r1 because \"the page shell, its script and the layout of the document root are mechanism, not program values; only the port, the canvases and the buttons come from the program\"\n0.8 r6 because \"the page markup cannot travel through an option value at all, so it lives in a clause that prints it\"\n0.95 d1 report <<<lips\nplaceholder, replaced below\nlips>>>\n"